# apps/web/.env.local — the Next app's environment. Copy to `.env.local` and fill in.
#
# Every variable here is OPTIONAL. With none of them set the site builds, renders
# and deploys: public pages fall back to committed data and the contact form
# offers a mailto link. The site has no sign-in of any kind; content is managed
# through the MCP server (packages/mcp), which authenticates against Convex with
# its own management credentials.
#
# The Convex *backend* is configured separately and NOT from this file. Anything
# a Convex function reads at runtime — GITHUB_TOKEN, OPENAI_API_KEY, … —
# lives in the Convex dashboard, because functions never see this repo's env
# files at all. See packages/convex/README.md for the full one-time setup order,
# and packages/convex/.env.example for the CLI's own local config.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ variables are inlined into the browser bundle at build time. Two
# consequences: they are public by definition (never put a secret behind that
# prefix), and changing one requires a rebuild, not a restart.


# ─── Site identity and index control ──────────────────────────────────────────

# The production origin. Everything absolute the site emits is built from this:
# `metadataBase` in the root layout (so every canonical link, Open Graph image
# and card URL resolves against it), every entry in /sitemap.xml, the `Sitemap:`
# and `Host:` lines in /robots.txt, and the `@id`s in the JSON-LD graph.
#
# OPTIONAL. Unset it defaults to https://coreybaines.com — ADR 017 settled the
# primary domain, so the default is the real answer rather than a placeholder,
# and a fresh checkout emits correct URLs with no environment at all.
#
# Set it deliberately to the *production* host even on a preview deployment.
# That is the point: a preview whose canonicals point at itself competes with
# the site it is previewing for the same search results. No trailing slash is
# needed (one is stripped if present).
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://coreybaines.com

# The index gate (ADR 018). Ships OFF, and every other value than the exact
# string `true` reads as off — a gate whose failure mode is "indexed the
# unfinished site under Corey's name mid-job-hunt" only gets to fail closed.
#
# While it is off:
#   • /robots.txt is `User-Agent: * / Disallow: /` and names no sitemap
#   • every page carries <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow">
#
# Set it EXACTLY ONCE, at cutover, on the PRODUCTION deployment — never on a
# preview, and never in a local .env.local. This is the switch that ends ADR
# 018's "build behind a preview URL while spiritdevs.com stays live" window, so
# flipping it is the launch, not a step towards it.
#
# It is inlined at build time (NEXT_PUBLIC_), so it takes effect on the next
# build rather than the next cold start. That is deliberate: a runtime read
# could flip between two ISR revalidations and leave half the prerendered HTML
# on the CDN saying noindex.
#
# `/admin` and `/api` are excluded from indexing
# unconditionally and are unaffected by this variable in either position.
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_INDEXABLE=true


# ─── Convex ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The deployment the browser client talks to, printed by `bunx convex dev` on
# first run and visible in the Convex dashboard.
#   dev:  https://<adjective-animal-000>.convex.cloud
#   prod: https://<adjective-animal-000>.convex.cloud (a different deployment)
#
# Required for any Convex read or write. The server reads it; no Convex client
# ships to the browser.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CONVEX_URL=


# ─── Uploadfile (ADR 020) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# The single credential Uploadfile needs, from uploadfile.dev → the application
# → API keys → Create API key. It is a base64 blob carrying the API key, app id,
# region and environment, and the SDK (`@uploadfile/core` 0.2.0 or later) picks
# the service address from it, which is why there is nothing else to set.
#
# SECRET. It authorises writes to file storage, so it must never gain a
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix and must never be imported by anything under
# src/components.
#
# Read at cold start by the contact form's Server Action (attachments) and the
# authenticated native upload route (`src/app/api/native/upload/route.ts`).
# Unset, the native route answers 503 with `{ error: "uploads-not-configured" }`
# and the contact form refuses attachments while still sending the message.
UPLOADFILE_TOKEN=


# ─── Ask Corey (ADR 015) ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ONE key runs the whole feature. It used to be two — OpenAI for embeddings,
# Anthropic for the answer — and the answering model has since moved to OpenAI,
# so `OPENAI_API_KEY` is now the only provider credential Ask Corey needs.
#
# It is still set in two places, because two *runtimes* read it and neither can
# see the other's environment:
#
#   ┌──────────────────────┬────────────────────────────┬────────────────────┐
#   │ where                │ read by                    │ for                │
#   ├──────────────────────┼────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┤
#   │ here / root .env     │ /api/ask in this app       │ the answer         │
#   │ Convex deployment    │ knowledge.ts, ask.ts       │ the embeddings     │
#   └──────────────────────┴────────────────────────────┴────────────────────┘
#
# Same key, copied to both. Setting it here does nothing for retrieval; setting
# it on Convex does nothing for answering. The full table, the exact commands
# and the one-time backfill are in packages/convex/README.md → "Ask Corey keys".
#
# Everything degrades honestly. With none of this set:
#   • the ask widget's panel says the model key is unset and points at the pages
#     that hold the content — no composer that fails after someone has typed a
#     question into it
#   • POST /api/ask answers 503 `{ configured: false, missing: [...] }` before
#     it spends anything, and names the variable it is waiting for
#   • retrieval still runs, still returns real citations, and reports
#     `retrievalMode: 'lexical'` so the UI can say the answer came from keyword
#     search rather than embeddings

# The key that answers — and, on the Convex side, the key that embeds. From
# platform.openai.com → API keys.
#
# SECRET — server-side only. It must never gain a NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, and
# nothing under src/components may import it. The (site) layout reads only a
# *boolean* derived from it (whether it is set) and passes that to the ask
# widget; the value itself never leaves the server.
#
# Read per request rather than at module scope, so setting it on a running
# deployment takes effect on the next question — no rebuild, no cold start.
#
# ⚠️ If you run through the repo's root scripts (`bun run dev`, which is
# `bun --env-file=.env run turbo run dev`), put it in the **root** .env and note
# that Turbo's strict environment mode only forwards variables named in
# turbo.json — `OPENAI_API_KEY` and `ASK_MODEL` are both listed under
# `globalPassThroughEnv` there. Adding a new runtime variable without adding it
# to that list produces a key that is set everywhere and visible nowhere.
OPENAI_API_KEY=

# Which model answers. OPTIONAL — defaults to `gpt-5.6-luna`, the cheap tier of
# the GPT-5.6 family, which is the right size for a concierge writing two to
# five sentences from five snippets that are already in the prompt.
#
# ⚠️ An **OpenAI** model id (`gpt-5.6-sol`, `gpt-5.6-terra`, `gpt-5.4-mini`, …).
# A leftover Anthropic id here will not be rejected locally — it 404s at OpenAI
# on the first question.
#
# Deliberately not validated against the provider's model-id union: that union
# is a snapshot of what existed when @ai-sdk/openai was published, and it ends
# in `(string & {})` precisely so a newer model can be named before the types
# catch up. A bad id fails at the provider with the provider's own error.
#
# ⚠️ The route pairs the model with `reasoningEffort: 'none'` and a 1024-token
# output ceiling. Point this at a model that has to think and both need raising
# in the same change, or answers will truncate.
#   ASK_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna

# The salt for the rate-limit identifier. Generate with:
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# SECRET, and the reason no raw IP address is stored anywhere in this system.
# src/lib/requestIdentity.ts hashes the caller's address with this salt and
# sends only the digest to Convex, which rejects anything that is not 64 hex
# characters. ADR 008: the address exists in this process for one function call
# and is never written down.
#
# Unset, the counters still work and still store no address — but the salt is
# then a constant, so a bucket key becomes computable by anyone who knows a
# visitor's IP. A warning is logged once per process. Set it in production.
RATE_LIMIT_SALT=
